course: dictionary
lesson: 4886
title: The little word if
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «If» is a small word with a big job. It joins two ideas and often sets a condition: what will happen when something else happens. «If it rains, we stay in.» The rain is the condition, and staying in is the result.
explain: «If» can also mean whether. «Ask if she can come» means ask whether she can come. Test it: swap in whether, and if the sentence still makes sense, that is the meaning.
explain: The words around «if» change its meaning. Look at «what if», «if only» and «as if». «What if pigs could fly?» is a pretend question. «If only I had a dog!» shows a strong wish. Read the whole phrase, not just one word.
explain: Writers also use «if» in serious rules and plans. «If you get lost, stand still and call for help» is a safety rule. «If something ever goes wrong in the air, two tough recorders called the black box help investigators» tells us what happens in an emergency.
fact: If is a conjunction, a joining word that links two parts of a sentence.
fact: «If» often links a condition to a result: if this happens, then that happens.
fact: «If» can mean whether, as in «Ask if she can come».
fact: «What if» asks about something imagined, and «if only» shows a strong wish.
fact: «As if» means as though: he acts as if he is the boss.
exercise: In «If it rains, we stay in», what does if show? | A wish for the rain to stop | *A condition: what happens when something else happens | A surprise about the weather | A question about who is at home
exercise: «Ask if she can come.» What does if mean here? | Because | *Whether | Only when she is ready | Very quickly
exercise: «If only I had a dog!» What does this show? | A safety rule | A sum of money | A question about the price of dogs | *A strong wish
test: «What if pigs could fly?» What is the sentence asking about? | The cost of a pig | *Something imagined | Something that happened yesterday | A rule for crossing the road
test: Your teacher says, «If you get lost, stand still and call for help.» What should you do, according to the rule? | Hide behind a tree | Keep walking in the dark | Run until you find home | *Stand still and call for help
exam: In «Should the price rise, we will tell you», what does should mean? | Must, because the price is high | Only after the price has gone up | Yes, the price has risen | *If, in the event that the price rises
